# Code owners for Lordpluha/bitrate
#
# Syntax is gitignore-like and THE LAST MATCHING PATTERN WINS, so the catch-all
# sits at the top and gets progressively narrowed below it. Only accounts with
# write access can be owners; today that is @Lordpluha, @andreo-kalashnello and
# @andreo-kalashnello.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# READ THIS BEFORE COMMITTING THE FILE
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The `develop` branch is protected with:
#
#     required_approving_review_count: 1
#     require_code_owner_reviews:      true
#     require_last_push_approval:      true
#     enforce_admins:                  false
#
# Right now `require_code_owner_reviews` is inert, because no CODEOWNERS file
# exists. Committing this file makes it real, and GitHub does not let anyone
# approve their own pull request. The consequence is concrete:
#
#   * A pull request touching a path owned by MORE THAN ONE person can be
#     approved by any other owner of that path. Those are fine.
#   * A pull request touching a path owned by @Lordpluha ALONE and opened by
#     @Lordpluha can never satisfy the code-owner requirement. It will sit
#     blocked until an admin bypasses the rule (`enforce_admins: false` allows
#     that) or the setting is turned off.
#
# The single-owner paths below are the CI, infra, agent-tooling and root-config
# blocks. That is not an accident — they should not be rubber-stamped — but it
# does mean every infrastructure pull request costs an admin bypass. The same
# applies to anything `/br-auto` opens on its own.
#
# So pick one deliberately:
#
#   a) Commit as-is and accept the bypass on infra/CI pull requests.
#   b) Add a co-owner to the single-owner blocks so someone can actually review.
#   c) Leave this file out and turn `require_code_owner_reviews` off instead,
#      which is the honest way to say "one approval from anyone is enough".
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

